#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/How-ROS-Works.rst:105
msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/How-ROS-Works.rst:107
msgid "What is a node in ROS?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/How-ROS-Works.rst:108
msgid ""
"A node is a modular software component within a ROS system that is "
"responsible for a specific task, such as controlling a motor or publishing "
"sensor data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/How-ROS-Works.rst:110
msgid ""
"A single executable can contain one or more nodes, and nodes communicate "
"with each other through defined ROS interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/How-ROS-Works.rst:112
msgid "How do ROS nodes communicate with each other?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/How-ROS-Works.rst:113
msgid ""
"ROS nodes exchange data through topics, services, and actions. Communication "
"between nodes is handled by the underlying middleware, which also supports "
"discovery across the ROS graph. Parameters configure individual nodes; they "
"are not a communication interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/How-ROS-Works.rst:117
msgid "Why should I learn the ROS CLI before creating my own nodes?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/How-ROS-Works.rst:118
msgid ""
"The ROS CLI helps you explore and understand a live ROS graph before writing "
"code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/How-ROS-Works.rst:120
msgid ""
"Using the command line tools allows you to inspect nodes, topics, services, "
"and other ROS elements, making it easier to understand how components "
"interact before using the ROS API to create your own applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/How-ROS-Works.rst:122
msgid "What is the ROS graph?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/How-ROS-Works.rst:123
msgid ""
"The ROS graph is the network of nodes in a ROS system and the relationships "
"between them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/How-ROS-Works.rst:125
msgid ""
"It represents how nodes communicate through topics, services, and actions, "
"and can be visualized using ROS tools such as ``rqt_graph``."
msgstr ""
